    "text": "<p>A massless square loop, of wire of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>,&nbsp;supporting a mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>,&nbsp;hangs vertically with one of its sides in a uniform magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math>, directed outwards in the shaded region. A dc&nbsp;voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is applied to the loop. For what value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math>, the magnetic force will exactly balance the weight of the supporting mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>?</p><p>(If sides of the loop <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0084_98d96de6d89d.png\" style=\"width: 149px; height: 200px;\" />.</p>"
